  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Given that the minor of ${d}_{12}$ is $-4$, find all the possible values of $p$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2} & {p}^{3} & 6 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2+p & p-1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we remove the first row and second column:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}\u2217 & {p}^{3} & \u2217 \\\\ -6 & \u2217 & 5 \\\\ 5 & \u2217 & p-1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${d}_{12}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 5 \\\\ 5 & p-1\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 5 \\\\ 5 & p-1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-6\\cdot (p-1)-5\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-6p-19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${d}_{12}$ is $-4$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6p-19 & =-4 \\\\ -6p & =15 \\\\ p & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $p=-\\frac{5}{2}.$",
